---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="From idea to business plan in 10 steps — Business Feasibility Toolkit"
  description="Check if your idea is worth it before you spend. 10 steps with free calculators. Finish with numbers for your study, plan, and pitch."
>
  <section class="rts-hero">
    <p class="rts-kicker"><span class="rts-badge-coral">Free</span> In English and Spanish</p>
    <h1>From idea to business plan, in 10 steps</h1>
    <p class="rts-lede">
      Most people lose money by spending before measuring.
      Here you check if your idea is worth it before you spend on it.
      Each step tells you what to find, where to find it, and which free calculator to use.
      At the end you decide with numbers and build your study, plan, and pitch.
    </p>
    <div class="rts-hero-actions">
      <a class="rts-btn" href="#steps">Start with step 1</a>
      <a class="rts-btn rts-btn-secondary" href={`${base}en/templates/`}>See what you will build</a>
    </div>
    <div class="rts-progress"><i id="bar"></i></div>
    <p class="rts-pct" id="pct">0% done</p>
  </section>

  <section class="rts-section">
    <h2 class="rts-section-h">How it works: from hunch to decision</h2>
    <p class="rts-sub">Not a course. A route to run your idea through numbers and finish with documents.</p>
    <div class="rts-grid3">
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">1 · Idea</span><h3>You start with an idea</h3><p>You write it down: problem, customer, what you sell. You talk to 5 to 10 possible customers.</p><span class="rts-go">Step 1 →</span></div>
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">2 · Numbers</span><h3>You run the numbers</h3><p>Market, cost, price, break-even, cash. If it needs more buyers than exist, you stop and save.</p><span class="rts-go">Steps 2 to 8 →</span></div>
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">3 · Documents</span><h3>You decide and write</h3><p>With written numbers, not excitement. If you go, you fill study, plan, summary and pitch.</p><span class="rts-go">Steps 9 and 10 →</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="rts-section" id="pasos">
    <h2 class="rts-section-h">The 10 steps, in order</h2>
    <p class="rts-sub">Do them in order. Each one fills part of your documents. There are two points where you can stop and save if numbers do not close.</p>
    <ol class="rts-steps" id="steps">
      <li data-step="1"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 1</p><h3>Write your idea</h3><p>Turn it into a 5-line sheet. See a vending example and what to ask.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> idea sheet.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/idea-sheet/`}>Fill my sheet →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="2"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 2</p><h3>Size your market</h3><p>Calculate TAM, SAM and SOM with a vending example. Free data sources included.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> market study.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/tam-sam-som/`}>Calculator →</a> <a href={`${base}en/guide/six-studies-methodology/`}>Step 2 guide →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="3"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 3</p><h3>Find your cost</h3><p>What each unit truly costs. Get 3 supplier quotes.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> technical study and costs.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/product-cost/`}>Calculator →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="4"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 4</p><h3>Set your price</h3><p>Covers costs, leaves profit, people pay it. Check 5 to 10 rivals.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> sales plan.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/pricing/`}>Calculator →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="5"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 5 · Early exit</p><h3>Break-even</h3><p>Units a month to stop losing.</p><p class="rts-exit">Compare with your market from step 2. If it needs more buyers than exist, it fails. Stop here.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> operations and finance.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/break-even/`}>Do it now →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="6"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 6</p><h3>Your cash</h3><p>What you need to start and whether it pays back.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> financial study.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/cash-flow/`}>Cash flow →</a> <a href={`${base}en/calculators/npv-irr/`}>NPV/IRR →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="7"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 7</p><h3>Each customer</h3><p>Each one should bring at least 3 times what they cost.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> sales and scenarios.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/cac-ltv/`}>Calculator →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="8"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 8 · Early exit</p><h3>Move the numbers</h3><p>Costs up 20% or fewer sales.</p><p class="rts-exit">If the plan cannot survive a 20% bad case, do not go on. Adjust or stop here.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> risks.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/calculators/sensitivity/`}>Calculator →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="9"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 9</p><h3>Legal check</h3><p>Taxes, trademark, permits. One session with an accountant.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> legal study and partners.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/guide/`}>Guide →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
      <li data-step="10"><div class="rts-step-card"><p class="rts-step-n">Step 10</p><h3>Decide: go or no</h3><p>With written numbers, not excitement. If go, write your papers.</p><p class="rts-papel"><strong>Fills:</strong> Go / No-Go decision.</p><p class="rts-links"><a href={`${base}en/templates/`}>Templates →</a></p><button type="button">Mark done</button></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="rts-section">
    <h2 class="rts-section-h">What you build at the end</h2>
    <p class="rts-sub">You finish with documents, not just ideas. Each template is in English and Spanish, Overleaf-ready.</p>
    <div class="rts-grid3">
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">Steps 1 to 9</span><h3>Feasibility study</h3><p>To decide with numbers if it can be done and last.</p></div>
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">Step 10</span><h3>Business plan</h3><p>To plan 3 to 5 years once you decide to go.</p></div>
      <div class="rts-card"><span class="rts-badge">For partners</span><h3>Summary and pitch</h3><p>2-page summary and 12 slides for banks and investors.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="rts-cta">
    <h2>Decide with numbers, not excitement</h2>
    <p>Start with step 1. If numbers do not close at step 5, you stop and save. If they close, you finish with study, plan, summary and pitch.</p>
    <p><a class="rts-btn rts-btn-secondary" href={`${base}en/templates/`}>See templates</a> <a class="rts-btn rts-btn-secondary" href="#steps">Start now</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
